{"status": "ok", "summary_markdown": "## Outcome\nThe run delivered a playable original single-file Three.js browser FPS (start briefing, 3 loadouts, HUD with minimap/compass/killfeed/hitmarker, 8 combat bots, ADS/fire/reload, HP plus armor plates, UAV unlock, shrinking zone, win/lose/restart) with 8 Warzone references recorded in PROGRESS.md, headless-Chrome verification with zero console errors, 7 inspected screenshots, a live public tunnel, and status comments on the issue. All workflow steps report success except Delivery, which had not yet run.\n\n## What worked\n- Research-first discipline: 8 references with stated purposes guided HUD layout, TTK, and match loop; shipped assets stayed original/procedural.\n- Real-artifact verification caught 5 genuine bugs: hitscan spread multiplier making aimed fire always miss, permanent recoil-pitch accumulation, spawn facing a wall, a POI pole filling the spawn view, and favicon 404s. All were fixed and re-verified (10 shots to 4 hits to 1 kill; enemy AI damaging the player unprompted).\n- A parallel session's stale-timer (runId guard) repair composed cleanly with the verification fixes; the agent checked the diff and grep counts before committing.\n- Deployment evidence was rigorous: entrypoint byte/title checks over HTTP, Pages build-status polling to `built`, and a full-DOM fetch of the public URL.\n\n## What did not work\n- The first goal completion was rejected for missing evidence, costing an extra continuation cycle.\n- Localhost networking friction: `localhost` requests hung repeatedly while `127.0.0.1` worked, and `tmux capture-pane` returned empty output, leaving server logs a blind spot.\n- Pages deployment confusion: two 404s before discovering the required `branches/<branch>/<sha>/` layout and the build-propagation delay, which required sleep-and-poll.\n- `app.log` shows the harness tried `npm start`, which does not exist for this static single-file game — workflow/project-shape mismatch.\n- Concurrent sessions on the same branch silently rewrote PROGRESS.md mid-run; the agent only noticed on edit conflict and had to re-read and append. Untracked files from the other session (e.g. package.json) were left in the tree.\n- No fresh-context critic/verifier was ever invoked despite the request explicitly requiring one; verification was single-agent self-review.\n- No true pointer-lock playthrough occurred; combat was driven via exposed test hooks, one public single-shot sample missed, and the victory screenshot shows synthetic forced stats (0% accuracy). The promised side-by-side capture-vs-reference comparison was never produced.\n\n## Root causes\n- Evidence-format requirements were learned by rejection rather than being specified up front in an actionable checklist.\n- Environment assumptions (localhost resolution, tmux logging, npm-start convention, Pages path layout) were never pre-validated; each was discovered through failure.\n- Single-branch multi-session execution had no file-ownership or merge protocol, inviting silent overwrites.\n- Testability was retrofitted (exposing camera/raycaster globals) instead of designed in, and determinism issues (wandering bots, recoil state) initially masqueraded as product bugs.\n\n## Prioritized improvements\n1. Pre-flight environment probe: resolve localhost vs 127.0.0.1, confirm log capture works, and confirm the serve/deploy path before building.\n2. Enforce the builder-plus-fresh-critic split the request demands; self-verification alone is insufficient.\n3. Design deterministic test hooks and seeded fixtures up front so gameplay verification does not depend on test-artifact luck.\n4. Establish a concurrent-session protocol (separate files or explicit re-read/merge) to prevent silent overwrites.\n5. Require at least one real-input playthrough trace and one side-by-side reference comparison before claiming the visual-fidelity bar is met.", "prompt_alignment": ["Require a machine-checkable evidence checklist (entrypoint, tests, screenshots, public URL, issue comment) so completion is accepted on the first attempt.", "Require a pre-flight probe of networking, logging, serve command, and deploy path before any implementation work begins.", "Mandate a fresh-context critic that inspects the running artifact independently; forbid self-verification as the only review.", "Require deterministic test hooks and seeded scenarios for gameplay verification rather than live-state-dependent assertions.", "Define a multi-session file-ownership rule: re-read shared status files before editing and never overwrite another session's evidence sections."], "skill_recommendations": [{"name": "gauntlet-loop", "action": "keep", "reason": "The builder-plus-harsh-critic loop it describes is exactly what this run skipped; prompt should invoke it explicitly for each major piece."}, {"name": "browser-verification", "action": "add", "reason": "No skill covers headless-browser game verification; the agent hand-rolled playwright scripts twice. A reusable harness (deterministic fixtures, state assertions, screenshot matrix) would remove the largest verification cost."}, {"name": "static-deploy", "action": "add", "reason": "Pages path-layout 404s and npm-start mismatch wasted cycles; a skill documenting static-artifact deploy conventions and pre-checks would prevent repeat friction."}]}
